# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 8 (a request goes out in the tick it fires) and ch. 9 (a forwarded element is the host's own at pos/[p]/0; a forwarding layer adds no tick and nests the path): the log stands at the child's label's key, 1/[0]/0 under the inner host and 0/[1/[0]/0]/0 under both, and its request is in the click's tick.
test one_host

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="go")
    1/[0]/0: Test.Log

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  requested:
    1/[0]/0: "went"

test two_hosts

tick 0
  added:
    0/[0]/0: Ui.Button(label="go")
    0/[1/[0]/0]/0: Test.Log

tick 1
  in:
    0/[0]/0: click
  requested:
    0/[1/[0]/0]/0: "went"
